1. Introduction to Linux
Linux is an open-source operating system used in computers, servers, cloud platforms, and networking devices.

Examples of Linux distributions:

-Ubuntu
-Kali Linux
-Debian
-Fedora
-Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL)
-Linux Mint

2. Methods of Accessing a Linux System
There are several ways to access a Linux system.

A. Physical Access
Directly access the computer using a keyboard, mouse, and monitor.

Log in using a valid username and password.

Access the desktop environment or command-line terminal.

B. Terminal Access
Open the terminal application.

Execute Linux commands to interact with the operating system.

Manage files, directories, users, and system settings.

C. SSH (Secure Shell) Access
SSH is a network protocol used to securely access a remote Linux system.
